  "notes": "SRVs (1C,1F,1G,1K,1L,1B) modeled as a single Component node representing the group of safety relief valves cycled during the event, since narrative treats them collectively rather than as individually distinct failure points. Previous similar event section only states 'turbine trip and reactor scram' with no LER number, plant, or unit given -- stub LER node created with key 'unknown' since no identifiable LER number was provided in the narrative to preserve per rule 9's requirement to use the exact stated LER number, though none was given here. Turbine bypass valve inhibit and turbine trip are modeled as parallel failure modes both stemming from loss of transmitter inputs, per rule 5 (single trigger causing two parallel failures)."
